closed identity gate, gambit refused — the wrapper protocol is Chez-tier)\"\n55:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-crypto/probes/run.clj\"\n58:  test:jolt-j5\n59:  {:doc \"J5 acceptance: one Python session through the JVM and jolt REPL entry points with the standard catalog (output equal line for line), the multiline probe sequence, and the unavailable-library REPL legs (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n61:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j5_acceptance.clj\")))}\n63:  probe:jolt-j5\n64:  {:doc \"J5b: the native Python parser's budget (input 4 MiB; in-parser guards: 8192 rule frames, 4096 SLL lookahead links, 256 full-LL links, on a 16 MiB parse thread): the review's repros, at/over per shape against the predicted table, 10x the old crash depths, the JVM's packets (incl. a 20,000-deep 1+ tree), the old crash depths in children on the jolt thread, injected C++ faults, the abort-is-a-failure property, lifecycle and unavailable-library legs. Args select legs: budget below crash inject abort unavailable (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n67:                         \"src/dev/jolt_j5_run.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n69:  calibrate:jolt-j5\n70:  {:doc \"J5b C4 + J5c: build the guards-off calibration variant of native/jolt-parser and record each nesting shape's stack cost per rule frame and per lookahead link on the 16 MiB parse thread (asserting every bound fits a quarter of the stack; writes build/j5b/calibration.edn), or, with --work, the work metric's per-shape counts and the corpus sweep the work bound derives from (writes build/j5b/work.edn; needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n73:                         \"src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n75:  probe:jolt-file\n76:  {:doc \"J4a: native/jolt-file gates, each in a child process: JVM-identical frame bytes (both hash algorithms), F2 s32BE prefixes, strict reads, injected short/EINTR/zero-progress/error transfers, corrupt-open byte identity, idempotent close, no fd or native-memory leak, a full collection during a 1 GiB :blocking pwrite, missing/wrong-layout wrapper refused before guest work, exported-symbol allowlist (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n78:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj\")))}\n80:  probe:jolt-udp\n81:  {:doc \"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n83:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\")))}\n85:  probe:jolt-udp-failures\n86:  {:doc \"J7 regression probe: native UDP setup failure injection, exception/buffer cleanup, fatal error seam closure, and receive diagnostics (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n88:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_failures_probe.sh\")))}\n90:  probe:jolt-tcp\n91:  {:doc \"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n96:                               (println \"== probe:jolt-tcp section\" s)\n98:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\n99:                                                \"jolt\" s))])\n101:           (println \"probe:jolt-tcp exits\" (pr-str results))\n104:  probe:jolt-ws\n105:  {:doc \"J6e: the jolt WebSocket host adapter (dao.stream.ws.jolt, the yin.repl.host shadow, the jolt -main wiring), one child jolt process per section: closure (C1), handshake (C2), bind (C3), address (C4), io (C5), close (C6), shutdown (C7, the real owner loop), isolation (C8), driver (C9, deadline folding, a --headless --port child), fairness (C10); native memory and registries empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n110:                               (println \"== probe:jolt-ws section\" s)\n112:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\n113:                                                \"jolt\" s))])\n115:           (println \"probe:jolt-ws exits\" (pr-str results))\n118:   workload-w:jolt\n119:   {:doc \"J6g: pre-registered Workload W, with an independent five-minute watchdog and ten-second sampler; one jolt worker serves two peers while stepping the REPL (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\n122:                          \"exec bb src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj \\\"$@\\\"\"\n123:                         \"jolt\" *command-line-args*)))}\n125:  build:jolt-native\n126:  {:doc \"Fetch (by pinned SHA-256, only when absent) and build the jolt-toolchain.edn :native sources with the mise-pinned CMake into build/native/<platform>/\"\n128:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_native.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n130:  test:jolt-host\n131:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n134:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.host.conformance-test dao.host.bytes-t