{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'trusted-prelude-modules|core-module/module-spec|register-library-module' src/cljc | head -100; cat src/cljc/yang/core/stage.cljc; cat mise.toml | head -90\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:443:(defn register-library-module\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:475:        (register-library-module 'kind kind-module kind-arities)\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:476:        (register-library-module\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4032:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4088:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4140:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc:178:                  (when (and (not= addr (get-in registry [:trusted-prelude-modules name]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc:192:   Trusted runtime identities are pinned by `:trusted-prelude-modules` in\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2620:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2744:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\n(ns yang.core.stage\n  \"The lowering stage every language shares (docs/design/yang.typescript.md\n   §17, lift L2): CST packets in, program batches on port `:program`,\n   diagnostics on port `:diagnostics`. A language supplies a `config`:\n\n     :diagnostic-ns   string, the namespace of its diagnostic keys\n     :program-medium  the program medium's default logical identity\n     :ok?             (fn [packet]) true when the packet is lowered\n     :lower           (fn [state packet]) the program tree of an ok packet\n     :option-keys     the state keys an options map may carry besides\n                      `:medium`\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]))\n\n\n(defn diagnostic\n  \"The record of a lowering diagnostic `data` for `unit`.\"\n  [diagnostic-ns unit data message]\n  (merge {:yang.cst/unit unit, :message message}\n         (select-keys data [(keyword diagnostic-ns \"diagnostic\") :rule\n                            :construct :span :name])))\n\n\n(defn lower-transform\n  \"The lowering stage's transform: an ok packet becomes one program batch on\n   port `:program`, a source envelope (`yin.vm.encoder/source-envelope`)\n   whose one member is the map AST `(:lower config)` returns, so its\n   `:yang/site` marks reach the frontend-metadata side table when the\n   encoder projects it. The medium is the state's `:medium` and the batch\n   token is the packet's unit. A packet that is not ok, or a lowering\n   diagnostic, becomes one record on port `:diagnostics` and no program.\n   Stateless.\"\n  [{:keys [diagnostic-ns program-medium ok? lower]} state packet]\n  (let [unit (:yang.cst/unit packet)\n        diagnostic-key (keyword diagnostic-ns \"diagnostic\")]\n    (if (ok? packet)\n      (try\n        [state [[:program (encoder/source-envelope\n                            (get state :medium program-medium)\n                            unit\n                            [(lower state packet)])]]]\n        ;; ClojureDart's ex-info type is not catchable by name portably;\n        ;; anything without a diagnostic in its ex-data is rethrown below\n        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                  :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo\n                  :cljs ExceptionInfo)\n               e\n          (if (get (ex-data e) diagnostic-key)\n            [state\n             [[:diagnostics\n               (diagnostic diagnostic-ns unit (ex-data e) (ex-message e))]]]\n            (throw e))))\n      [state\n       [[:diagnostics {:yang.cst/unit unit,\n                       diagnostic-key (keyword diagnostic-ns\n                                               (name (:yang.cst/outcome\n                                                       packet))),\n                       :errors (:yang.cst/errors packet)}]]])))\n\n\n(defn open-stage\n  \"A lowering stage reading CST packets from `cst-stream`, writing program\n   batches to `program-stream`, whose logical identity is `medium`, and\n   diagnostics to `diagnostics-stream`. The fourth argument may instead be\n   an options map of `:medium` and the config's `:option-keys`; the fifth,\n   `max-digits`, is the digit budget of every packet that declares none.\"\n  ([config cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream]\n   (open-stage config\n               cst-stream\n               program-stream\n               diagnostics-stream\n               (:program-medium config)))\n  ([{:keys [program-medium option-keys]}\n    cst-stream\n    program-stream\n    diagnostics-stream\n    medium-or-opts]\n   (stage/open cst-stream\n               {:program program-stream, :diagnostics diagnostics-stream}\n               (if (map? medium-or-opts)\n                 (let [{:keys [medium], :or {medium program-medium}}\n                       medium-or-opts]\n                   (assoc (select-keys medium-or-opts option-keys)\n                          :medium medium))\n                 {:medium medium-or-opts})))\n  ([_config cst-stream program-stream diagnostics-stream medium max-digits]\n   (stage/open cst-stream\n               {:program program-stream, :diagnostics diagnostics-stream}\n               {:medium medium, :max-digits max-digits})))\n\n\n(defn step-stage\n  [config s]\n  (stage/step s (partial lower-transform config)))\n[tools]\njava = [\"21\", \"17\"]\ncljstyle = \"0.17.642\"\nzprint = \"1.3.0\"\nbabashka = \"1.13.225\"\nclojure = \"1.12.4.1602\"\nnode = \"25.6.1\"\n# jolt host lane (jolt-toolchain.edn): exact pins, never \"latest\"; a change of\n# either goes through the jolt upgrade gate\nchezscheme = \"10.4.1\"\n# gambit is not in mise's registry; the asdf plugin joeljuca/asdf-gambit builds\n# the v4.9.8 tag from source (pre-generated C in the tag archive, so no\n# gambit bootstrap step) — the same from-source 4.9.8 jolt's CI gates target\n# (Makefile GAMBIT_PREFIX comment; tests.yml). Plugin pinned to its full HEAD\n# SHA (mise rejects abbreviated ones). Never \"latest\".\n# Known divergence (review 1794970000000 P2-1): the plugin configures with\n# --enable-single-host only; jolt CI (tests.yml) additionally passes\n# --enable-default-runtime-options=f8,-8,t8. Gates pass with the plugin build;\n# revisit at the upgrade gate if a gate ever disagrees.\n# Fresh installs run a ~15-20 min from-source build including the plugin's\n# `make check` (review P2-2); Linux verified once before this pin landed.\n# [plugins] must stay the LAST table in this file — a mid-file table broke\n# mise's validation of the flutter entry (engineer findings 1794934400000).\ngambit = \"4.9.8\"\ncmake = \"4.4.4\"\nandroid-sdk = \"latest\"\nflutter = { version = \"3.47.8\", platforms = \"\"\"\n[linux-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/linux/flutter_linux_{{ version }}-beta.tar.xz\"\n\n[macos-arm64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_arm64_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\n[macos-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\n[windows-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/windows/flutter_windows_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\"\"\", version_json_path = \".releases[?channel=beta].version\", version_list_url = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/releases_macos.json\" }\n\n[env._]\npath = [\n  \"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/platform-tools\",\n  \"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/emulator\",\n]\n\n[env]\n#FLUTTER_STORAGE_BASE_URL = \"https://storage.flutter-io.cn\"\n#PUB_HOSTED_URL = \"https://pub.flutter-io.cn\"\n\n[plugins]\ngambit = \"https://github.com/joeljuca/asdf-gambit#b8a901e7af845c8b0a0ee1adc5b67687ba4c582b\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; cat test/yang/clojure/donor_link_test.clj | head -170; sed -n '4000,4150p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; cat test/yang/clojure/donor_link_test.clj | head -170; sed -n '4000,4150p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.python.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the Python tests (C4 slices P2\n   and P3, docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): the namespace that requires\n   this is the publisher of `py` and `pysp`, so it publishes each module\n   once per process into one in-memory content store and serves them to\n   every linked run over a `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under\n   `:trusted` derivation (the remediation ruling's R6). The `:verifying`\n   evidence is `publish-module!`'s own `link-local` links, which\n   `linked-prelude-test` asserts.\n\n   A linked run builds the program's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately\n   until the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker\n   is not a backend here: its link of `py` is refused `:undeclared-free`\n   until L-b.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n  \"The ordinary Python composition's `integer` limits.\"\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The full host registry a linked Python composition registers: the\n   `require` handler, then `cell`, `data`, `integer` under `limits`, and\n   `stream` — the hook module `pysp` polls a signal stream, so the\n   safepointed composition needs it even though `py` does not.\"\n  ([] (registry integer-limits))\n  ([limits]\n   (-> (module/default-registry)\n       module/register-cell-module\n       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n       module/register-stream-module)))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`yang.call` and `py` published once into their own content store.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n          result (publish/publish-module! store\n                                          (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                               (:address call-result)))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result),\n       :call-result call-result, :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n\n\n(def published-pysp\n  \"`pysp` published once into `py`'s own content store, which its pinned\n   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n          result (publish/publish-module!\n                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` defaults\n   to `{py <address> yang.call <address>}`, derivation `:trusted`, the test being the\n   publisher. Explicit name environments also receive the harness's\n   `yang.call` runtime module, which every linked Python body requires.\n   `pysp`-serving sources pass their own `name-env`, the\n   safepointed runs' `{'py a :pysp b}` both.\"\n  ([] (source {'py (:address @published),\n               'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n  ([name-env]\n   (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n                      :name-env (merge {'yang.call (:call-address @published)}\n                                       name-env),\n                      :derivation :trusted})))\n\n\n(defn safepoint-source\n  \"The serving composition for `pysp`, `py`, and the `yang.call` module\n   required by `py`.\"\n  []\n  (source {'py (:address @published), 'pysp (:address @published-pysp),\n           'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n\n\n(defn publish-guest-module!\n  \"One guest module's `spec` (lower/module-spec's) published into `py`'s\n   own content store, where its pinned requirements already live:\n   `publish-module!`'s answer. The test helper supplies the harness's\n   `yang.call` address as the runtime dependency when a test constructs a\n   spec directly. Guest modules are tiny beside `py`, so a test may publish\n   its own; publish imports bottom-up, the `deps` map naming each import's\n   address.\"\n  [spec]\n  (publish/publish-module! (:store @published)\n                           (update spec :requires\n                                   #(assoc (or % {}) 'yang.call\n                                           (:call-address @published)))))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(def continues\n  \"Each vector backend's admission of the next top-level unit to a halted\n   task, as `yin.repl` admits an input line: the task keeps its store,\n   heap, module registry and module stores.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [task ast]\n               (semantic/load-ast task (vm/ast->datoms ast) vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [task ast]\n            (let [img (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                  attached (dvm/attach-image task img vm/stack-contract)]\n              (assoc attached\n                     :pc (dvm/absolute-pc attached [(dcode/image-hash img) 0])\n                     :frames [] :stack [] :continuation []\n                     :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil))),\n   :register (fn [task ast]\n               (let [img (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                     attached (rvm/attach-image task img vm/register-contract)\n                     pc (rvm/absolute-pc attached\n                                         [(rcode/register-hash img) 0])\n                     body (some #(when (= pc (:start %)) %)\n                                (:bodies (:segment attached)))]\n                 (assoc attached\n                        :pc pc :frames [] :continuation []\n                        :registers (vec (repeat (:registers body) nil))\n                        :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin))),\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules modules,\n   :link-request (:requests pair),\n   :link-response (:responses pair)})\n\n\n(defn drive\n  \"Run `task` and serve `pair` from `src` alternately until the task\n   stops blocking, at most 40 rounds. Returns `[task pair]`.\"\n  [task pair src]\n  (loop [task (vm/run task)\n         pair pair\n         i 0]\n    (if (and (vm/blocked? task) (< i 40))\n      (let [pair (:pair (link/serve {:pair pair, :source src}))]\n        (recur (vm/run task) pair (inc i)))\n      [task pair])))\n\n\n(defn run-linked\n  \"The finished task of the linked program `ast` on `backend`. Options:\n   `:modules` (default the full registry), `:link-source` (default the\n   `:trusted` composition over `py`), and `:prep`, applied to the task\n   before it runs (a composition handing the task its streams, binding\n   `pysp`'s signal stream among them). A refused link throws as the task's\n   own error.\"\n  ([backend ast] (run-linked backend ast {}))\n  ([backend ast {:keys [modules link-source prep]}]\n   (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n         task ((get backends backend)\n               ast\n               (composition (or modules (registry)) pair))]\n     (first (drive (if prep (prep task) task)\n                   pair (or link-source (source)))))))\n\n\n(defn runners-under\n  \"Each vector VM's runner of a linked program over `modules`: the\n   program's value.\"\n  [modules]\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [k]\n               [k (fn [ast]\n                    (vm/value (run-linked k ast {:modules modules})))]))\n        (keys backends)))\n\n\n(def runners\n  \"The linked runners under the ordinary limits.\"\n  (runners-under (registry)))\n(ns yang.clojure.donor-link-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [yang.clojure :as clj]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.core.module :as module]\n            [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yang.rt.effect :as effect]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]))\n\n\n(deftest linked-donor-uses-runtime-context\n  (let [{:keys [store call-address]} @h/published\n        registry (prelude/admit (h/registry))\n        effect-address (:address (h/publish-guest-module! (effect/module-spec registry)))\n        runtime (h/publish-guest-module! (prelude/module-spec registry call-address effect-address))\n        unit (clj/lower-unit '[(defn f [x] (try (throw x) (catch Exception e e)))\n                               (f 42)])\n        ast (u/annotate-call-sites\n              (module/module-tree [(module/require-node 'clj) (u/def! 'body unit)]))\n        spec (module/module-spec :test/refusal :test/undeclared registry\n                                 {:name 'test.clj-donor :ast ast :exports '#{body}\n                                  :runtime-name 'clj :runtime-address (:address runtime)\n                                  :deps {'yang.call call-address}})\n        donor (h/publish-guest-module! spec)\n        caller-ast (u/annotate-call-sites\n                     (module/module-tree\n                       [(module/require-node 'clj)\n                        (module/require-node 'test.clj-donor)\n                        (u/def! 'run (u/sexp->uast\n                                       '(fn [] (clj/run-main test.clj-donor/body))))]))\n        caller (h/publish-guest-module!\n                 (module/module-spec :test/refusal :test/undeclared registry\n                                     {:name 'test.caller :ast caller-ast :exports '#{run}\n                                      :runtime-name 'clj :runtime-address (:address runtime)\n                                      :deps {'test.clj-donor (:address donor)}}))\n        source (link/composition\n                 {:content-store store :derivation :trusted\n                  :name-env {'clj (:address runtime) 'yang.call call-address\n                             'yrt.effect effect-address\n                             'test.clj-donor (:address donor) 'test.caller (:address caller)}})\n        program (u/sexp->uast '(do (require 'test.caller) (test.caller/run)))]\n    (is (contains? prelude/module-exports 'rt-ctx))\n    (is (some? (:address donor)) (pr-str donor))\n    (is (some? (:address caller)) (pr-str caller))\n    (is (not (contains? (core/free-names unit) 'clj.rt/ctx)))\n    (is (contains? (core/free-names unit) 'clj/run-source-unit))\n    (doseq [backend [:semantic :stack :register]]\n      (is (= 42 (vm/value (h/run-linked backend program {:modules registry :link-source source})))\n          (str backend)))))\n                             builtin-functions))]\n                ;; sys.modules and its two pre-seeded modules (C4 I1):\n                ;; `sys`, whose dict holds the dict itself under modules,\n                ;; and `builtins`, whose dict IS the builtins namespace\n                ;; with the standard dunders in it\n                [(define 'py.rt/modules '(py/dict-new))\n                 (define 'py.rt/sys '(py/module-new (py/str \"sys\") :py/None))\n                 (list 'py/dict-set '(py/module-dict py.rt/sys)\n                       {:py/str \"modules\"} 'py.rt/modules)\n                 (define 'py.rt/builtins-mod '(py/module-of \"builtins\"\n                                                            py.b/builtins))\n                 (list 'py/dict-set 'py.b/builtins\n                       {:py/str \"__name__\"} '(py/str \"builtins\"))\n                 (list 'py/dict-set 'py.b/builtins\n                       {:py/str \"__package__\"} :py/None)\n                 (list 'py/dict-set 'py.b/builtins\n                       {:py/str \"__spec__\"} :py/None)\n                 (list 'py/dict-set 'py.b/builtins\n                       {:py/str \"__loader__\"} :py/None)\n                 (list 'py/modules-put! (list 'py/str \"sys\") 'py.rt/sys)\n                 (list 'py/modules-put! (list 'py/str \"builtins\")\n                       'py.rt/builtins-mod)]\n                [(define 'py.rt/importlib '(py/module-new (py/str \"importlib\")\n                                                          (py/str \"\")))\n                 (list 'py/dict-set '(py/module-dict py.rt/importlib)\n                       {:py/str \"import_module\"} 'py.b/import-module)\n                 (list 'py/dict-set '(py/module-dict py.rt/importlib)\n                       {:py/str \"reload\"} 'py.b/reload)\n                 (list 'py/modules-put! (list 'py/str \"importlib\") 'py.rt/importlib)]\n                ;; last, so a failed init never reports ready\n                [(define 'py.rt/state :py/ready)\n                 :py/None])\n              :py/None)))\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order:\n   every prelude function, the literal state slot, then `py/init!`. Defining\n   them runs nothing.\"\n  (into core-definitions\n        [['py.rt/state :py/uninit]\n         ['py/init! (init-form)]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private definitions->uast core/definitions->uast)\n\n\n(def functions-uast\n  \"The shared call runtime followed by every Python definition. Defining\n   them runs nothing, so this loads on any composition, with or without cells.\"\n  (definitions->uast (into call/definitions definitions)))\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled prelude: every definition, then the task's runtime state\n   allocated by `py/init!`.\"\n  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(py/init!))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `py`\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module the Python runtime profile is published as.\"\n  'py)\n\n\n(def runtime-keys\n  \"Every key `py/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted: the four\n   runtime cells, the builtin classes, functions and method\n   implementations, the builtins dict, and sys.modules with its three\n   pre-seeded module objects. Read from the same tables `init-form` reads.\"\n  (vec (sort-by str\n                (concat '[py.rt/ctx py.rt/limit py.rt/out py.rt/value py.b/builtins\n                          py.rt/modules py.rt/sys py.rt/builtins-mod py.rt/importlib]\n                        (mapv second builtin-classes)\n                        (mapv second builtin-functions)\n                        (mapv first method-implementations)))))\n\n\n(defn strip\n  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `py`; any other value as it\n   is. `py.b/*` and `py.rt/*` stay qualified: they are internal store keys,\n   and stripping them would collide (`py/list` and `py.b/list`).\"\n  [sym]\n  (core/strip \"py\" sym))\n\n\n(def ^:private module-definitions\n  \"The module's definition list: a `:py/uninit` placeholder for every\n   runtime key, so each read of one is discharged by an unconditional\n   module-level definition, then every definition, stripped.\"\n  (core/module-definitions \"py\" :py/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  \"The module tree: one application whose operands are the definitions,\n   in order, followed by `require yang.call`, applied to a lambda that\n   returns nil. Every definition runs on the main sequence before the\n   require, so the linker's scanners discharge every body read of a sibling\n   or runtime key. Defining runs nothing.\"\n  (core/module-tree module-definitions\n                    [(u/sexp->uast '(require (quote yang.call)))]))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The module's exports: every `py/` key of the definition list,\n   stripped. The runtime keys and the state slot are internal.\"\n  (core/exports \"py\" definitions))\n\n\n(def free-names\n  \"Every variable name some occurrence of the map AST reads unbound by an\n   enclosing lambda.\"\n  core/free-names)\n\n\n(def defined-keys\n  \"Every literal key the map AST defines with `yin/def`, at any depth.\"\n  core/defined-keys)\n\n\n(def ^:private module-free-names\n  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the\n   primitives and the host exports its manifest must declare.\"\n  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `py`\n   over the host registry `registry`. Every free name of the module tree\n   is declared under `:primitives`; a free name nothing supplies is\n   refused before anything is published. This namespace emits; it never\n   publishes.\"\n  [registry call-address]\n  (prelude-admission/module-spec\n    {:module-name module-name,\n     :ast module-uast,\n     :exports module-exports,\n     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n     :free-names module-free-names,\n     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n     :registry registry,\n     :message \"the py module reads an undeclared name\",\n     :refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}))\n\n\n(def min-integer-bits\n  \"The smallest `::integer/max-bits` this profile admits: every inline\n   literal (up to 2^53 - 1) must fit (C3 S2).\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
