urface ledger; §2 gains the tao-architecture second-axiom alignment (the semantics descriptor is stream-resident interpreter configuration; the provenance tuple names the interpreter).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:20:**Scope, Owner Clean-Slate Directive, and amendments:** This document settles owner decision A12.5 of `yang.typescript.md` §19 (the deferred `yrt` shared prelude lift) and extends `yang.antlr.md` §3.1/§3.4/§9.3 to treat preludes as **composable runtime modules** and **swappable frontend libraries** supporting both **native language profiles** (for existing Python, TypeScript, PHP, and Clojure programs) and **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (allowing familiar syntaxes such as `yang.python` or `yang.typescript` to compile directly onto `clojure.core` and persistent Yin data). Per the Owner Clean-Slate Directive (single-user system, zero legacy deployments), clean rewrites, uniform emitter normalization, direct `yang.clojure` migration onto `clojure.core`, and clean golden regeneration are explicitly preferred over maintaining dual legacy runtimes or frozen-quirk compatibility shims. It adds no UAST node type, no VM opcode, no manifest schema version, and no closed language registry.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:636:Per the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, regenerate affected golden snapshots cleanly per slice (`P0`–`P4`) and validate correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and CPython/Node/PHP language-oracle parity suites.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:649:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); the cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind gate — cleanup and context restoration, exactly once per activation — listed directly here; capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:40:| C4 scanner pins `[:c4 :py]` / `[:c4 :t]` in `test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc` stale since I4-a; slow `scan-test` bodies fail on master until regenerated | follow-up-1 / owner scheduling | yang.python seat / muse | closed 2026-10-17: regenerated via the checked-in generator (`scanner-golden-c4.generate.clj`, abort-gated on all untouched groups, byte-identical double-run); Fable review (claude-api lane) READY. Recurred after C4 I1 (aad451c5e moved `:pysp`): re-closed same day at 37db44da with her corrected provenance; standing rule added to the generator header — any slice touching the prelude, safepoint, lowering or import programs runs the generator in